A||||10||Supernaut||86 GT Rescue||||6||
Z||000000||Supernaut||06-30-2000||11:46 PM||||I found this sitting behind a barn on the windswept Texas high plains a few weeks ago, and brought it home today.  Here are some pics I took just after we unloaded her off the trailer!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/f63000.jpg"> <P>When I first saw it, I approached the owner to see if he was interested in selling and he told me he'd take $900 for it.  I left my phone number with him and he called last night to let me know he had reconsidered and we settled on a figure of $500  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I have big plans for this car...it will take a lot of work and several parts (appears to have been run under the rear bumper of another vehicle) and I am eager to get started on the body disassembly.<P>This is my first post on this forum, and I want to thank you all for sharing your knowlege and experience here as it will be of great help to me as I begin this project.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000001||snowkttn||06-30-2000||11:54 PM||||Hi Supernaut......I too am new here....I own a 86 GT fastback as well, black.......I look forward to seeing how you progress on getting your Fiero in shape.......looks pretty good though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">))||||reg||12
Z||000002||Coconut||07-01-2000||04:52 PM||||Anyone who is willing to rescue an '86 GT is alright by me! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Welcome aboard pal. As you progress on this project, I'm sure you'll get alot of satisfaction out of fixing it up.<BR>Judging from the pics, it seems to be in fairly decent shape other than the obvious damage you previously mentioned. Is this your first Fiero? Anyhow, Good Luck and if ya need anything, from Tech Answers to Moral Support, we'll be here!<P>Cruisin' On,<BR>Coconut  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Larry F.<BR>Black '86 GT||||reg||14
Z||000003||Cooter||07-01-2000||06:31 PM||||Supernaut,<BR> Look close at the front edge of the engine hood- is there a rubber seal attached to it where it meets the rear window? It is hard to see in your pictures. Also, is there a tube from the front bank valve cover that hooks into the rubber pipe on the throttle body? It looks like you new toy has not had the recall work done on it. Lucky for you!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Supernaut||07-01-2000||09:03 PM||||Thanks Cooter for the sharp eye!  <P>It appears none of the recall work has been done at all on this vehicle.  I read the recent thread on the recall subject and it looks like I'll be hitting the dealership(s) here soon.  This could be sweet payback in a sense...I bought the first 1984 SE Fiero to make it to this part of Texas at the tender age of 16.  It was one of a kind around here for quite a while, red and gorgeous.  Unfortunately every malady known to that model hit within the first six months I owned it (except the self-immolation thing) and the dealer sevice centers here were unable to correct anything!  That car spent more time in the warranty ward than it did enhancing my newfound manhood.  Needless to say, I rid myself of her after one year and the service managers rejoiced.  I swore off Pontiacs for a long time after that experience and went on to trash several other vehicles of different origin before reaching maturity  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Last year, I ran a cross a blue/silver 87 GT and bought it, very used but it ran good and had a lot of potential.  I throughly enjoyed this Fiero experience and it certainly rekindled my love for the little car.  Unfortunately, a friend borrowed it to run to the store last september, ran a red light and totaled it. grrrrr<P>This one is to be my baby, I plan to refurbish and refinish every nook and cranny and end up with as fresh a vehicle as I can hope for.  And no, I will not be loaning it to any friends.<P>I'll be posting regular updates on my progress here and will try not to bug you too much with dumb questions.<P>Thanks again!||||reg||10
Z||000005||bHooper||07-01-2000||09:37 PM||||Congrats!  Speaking from experience ( i just brought my own GT back to life) you have a big job ahead of you!  but it will be rewarding!  does the car run?  how many miles does it have on it?<P>b4 you take it in to the dealer for recall work, you might want to remove that seal (on the back of the deck)... they are valuable!<P>enjoy, and keep posting pics!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bill Osmer||07-01-2000||10:40 PM||||Congratulations, from another '86 GT owner. <P>It doesn't look like you've got too serious a job ahead - although lots of cleaning and detailing. When that's done, you WILL know every nook and cranny. Follow the advice given here on the Forum, and you'll have her lookin' like new before the summer's out!!<P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR>'86 Silver GT Fastback<p>[This message has been edited by Bill Osmer (edited 07-01-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000007||TheFiero64||07-02-2000||10:12 PM||||Great save. ||||reg||10
Z||000008||FIEROCIOUS||07-03-2000||03:11 AM||||Were are all these $500.00 Fieros hideing?<BR>Every one around here wants an arm and a leg for even the squirliest Fiero! Man I hope my lucky day comes soon! LOL!<P>Welcome to the forum!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Child Of Rod||07-03-2000||09:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FIEROCIOUS:<BR>[B]Were are all these $500.00 Fieros hideing?<BR>Every one around here wants an arm and a leg for even the squirliest Fiero! Man I hope my lucky day comes soon! LOL!<BR>B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Heh..I found 2 $500 Fieros, and one $300  84 Fiero in my area.  They need work....and titles.  All of them run now, even the one that was sitting for 10 years.  One of the $500 ones is an 86se with t-tops...it's just needs a title.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000010||TheFiero64||07-03-2000||10:27 AM||||I got my 88 for $400<BR>an 86 SE v6 and a 85 coupe $500 for both<BR>and my 86 GT for $1000||||reg||10
